--
N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/1, [temp.constr.decl], [temp.arg.type]:
impl<int, long> selects the constrained partial specialization, whose
`type' is long; that type is a valid template argument of any template.
As an argument of a class template it works; as an argument of the
variable template is_long the front end fails to type-check it and
reports "found no match for symbol 'is_long'" (with no candidates: the
argument list's failure is swallowed in resolve's variable-template
path).  Without the requires-clause it works.  cvise reduction
(/tmp/r163/red/kb_L16cr) of libstdc++ 16's
`is_same_v<common_reference_t<int &, long &>, long>'
(cpp20_common_reference_int_lvalue_rvalue with GCC 16's headers).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept the program.  Pre-existing (fails on bin53).
